at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-10-24T12:37:50Z","updated_at":"2025-10-25T12:17:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\n### Tested versions\n\n1. godot v4.5\n2. godot v4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nAndroid 15 - GODOT v4.5.1\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen switching to right-to-left (direction layout) in settings editor, Problems occur in the following nodes: \n1. Canveslayer: The elements inside are flipped in the opposite direction.\n2. TileMap: When you add an image and want to crop it to extract the tiles, you cannot move to the left, and if you do, everything will disappear and you cannot go back. This also happens when zooming in and out, as the preview takes you to a place where you cannot do anything, which forced me to convert the layout to LTR. When I finished, I returned the layout to (RTL) and found that the tiles had been deleted.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nTo repeat the problem, follow the following:\n1. Switch your editor settings to a language that supports right-to-left layout or set the layout direction to right-to-left.\n2. Add a node TileMap Add an image and try to preview it by moving it.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https: